# LD-040 secret scan, 2026-10-24. gitleaks 8.30.1 (the version CI pins; local binary ~/tools/gl/gitleaks,
# sha256 88f91962aa2f93ac6ab281d553b9e125f5197bbbce38f9f2437f7299c32e5509, extracted from the CI-pinned
# gitleaks_8.30.1_linux_x64.tar.gz 551f6fc8...70eb).
# Scope: every branch of origin. `git fetch origin --prune` brought all 49 remote branches (refs/remotes/origin/*,
# develop at 19ad538, main, every feature/fix/qa/docs/chore branch and every open PR head) into this repository; the
# agent sandbox refuses a separate `git clone --mirror` outside its worktree, so the fetched refs stand in for the
# mirror. Not covered: refs/pull/* of closed, deleted-branch PRs.
# The repository's .gitleaksignore applies (3 fingerprints, each with a reason; see SECURITY-BASELINE.md §3).

$ git fetch origin --prune
$ git for-each-ref refs/remotes/origin | wc -l
50   (49 branches + origin/HEAD)
$ gitleaks detect --source . --redact --no-banner --exit-code 1 --log-opts=--all
INF 135 commits scanned.
INF scanned ~28315908 bytes (28.32 MB) in 21.8s
INF no leaks found
(exit 0)

